  "_commit": {
    "id": "7a002943a9606eb37e2ec15bafe1ca07b0830fdd",
    "author": "Arek Gladki <41166437+gladkia@users.noreply.github.com>",
    "committer": "GitHub <noreply@github.com>",
    "message": "ci: require the macOS and Windows jobs to pass (M3) (#136)\n\nThe matrix carried allow-failure on macOS and Windows since the R 4.5/4.6\nversion mismatch was mistaken for shinytest2 flakiness. That root cause was\nfixed in #123 (r: '4.6' on both), and the jobs have since run green \u2014 the last\n12 consecutive check-bioc runs (2026-07-25, 6 distinct SHAs, push and\npull_request) succeeded on the full matrix, with mac/win producing a complete\nBiocCheck 0 ERROR / 0 WARNING / 2 NOTES.\n\nDropping the flags makes 'CI green on Linux, macOS and Windows' an enforced\ncondition rather than a reported one, which is the M3 deliverable.\n\nRelated: #129",
    "time": 1785044108
  },
